  "question": {
    "text": "Let $f: \\mathbb{R} \\rightarrow \\mathbb{R}$ be a function defined by\n$f(x)=(2+3 a) x^2+\\left(\\frac{a+2}{a-1}\\right) x+b, a \\neq 1 . \\text { If }$ \n$f(x+\\mathrm{y})=f(x)+f(\\mathrm{y})+1-\\frac{2}{7} x \\mathrm{y}$, then the value of $28 \\sum_{i=1}^5|f(i)|$ is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "hKQke",
      "text": "545",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "GxmH7",
